  "metadata": {
    "synthetic": true,
    "source": "synthetic, for demonstration",
    "origin": "Synthetic demonstration values of docs/domains/PRODUCTION_LOGISTICS.md (H-045, H-046): realistic structure and magnitudes from the sources listed there, scaled; NOT customer data, plant measurements or any company's data.",
    "assumptions": [
      "Time unit minute; t=0 is Monday 00:00 model time (no time zone).",
      "Two shifts 06:00-14:00 and 14:00-22:00, Monday to Friday; 9 receivers (three trailer crews) early and 3 late, 4 pickers early and 3 late.",
      "One item is a case. Five floor-loaded inbound trailers of 1,200 cases arrive every 90 min from 06:00 to 12:00 on weekdays (6,000 cases a day).",
      "Unloading takes about 0.6 receiver-minutes a case (a crew of three empties a trailer in about four hours).",
      "Case picking is the bottleneck: tri(0.35, 0.45, 0.75) min a case, about 116 cases an hour a picker with travel included, about 90% busy on shift. Pick paths are not modelled.",
      "Orders are assumed to be waiting for every stored case, so picking is limited by pickers, not by orders; reserve storage holds 6,000 cases, and a full storage blocks put-away.",
      "Put-away takes pallets of 24 to 48 cases (at most 20 min wait to fill once 24 are waiting), tri(3, 4, 6) min a pallet with three reach trucks that break down.",
      "The scan and weight check finds a pick error in 0.3% of cases (a model input); the problem solver corrects and re-packs them.",
      "Outbound trailers load 600 to 1,200 cases (at most 60 min wait to fill once 600 are waiting), tri(30, 45, 60) min a trailer at two dock doors.",
      "Breakdowns count on-shift time only; the time to failure and repair parameters are estimates."
    ]
  }
